{
    "background_story": "Lincoln was a free-spirited artist who lived life on his own terms. Growing up in a world where everyone seemed to be chasing perfection, he rebelled against the idea of being polished and refined. Lincoln's art was a reflection of his unprocessed nature - raw, emotive, and unapologetic. He rejected the conventional norms of the art world, instead choosing to create pieces that were honest and unbridled. His studio was a haven for like-minded individuals who sought to express themselves without the constraints of societal expectations. Lincoln's unprocessed approach to life and art inspired a movement, encouraging others to shed their pretenses and embrace their true selves. His mantra, ' Imperfections are what make us beautiful,' became a rallying cry for those seeking authenticity in a world of curated perfection.",
